      "id": "https://thenextweb.com/news/claude-install-as-app-artifacts-mac-windows-desktop",
      "url": "https://thenextweb.com/news/claude-install-as-app-artifacts-mac-windows-desktop",
      "title": "Anthropic lets Claude users install AI-built apps on Mac and Windows",
      "content_html": "Anthropic has begun beta testing a feature that turns interactive tools made with its Claude AI assistant, known as artifacts, into desktop apps for Mac and Windows with their own icons and windows. Users can share the apps, and edits to an underlying tool update its installed app. The feature is rolling out across Claude plans but requires the desktop app, an internet connection and a signed-in Claude account.\n\nThe apps can use Claude and connected services, with requests counting against a user’s plan limits. Permissions range from browser-like access to the ability to run programs and read, change or delete files without asking each time. Anthropic says it does not review apps before installation and warns users to grant full access only to apps whose creators they trust.\n\nUsers can open installed tools without finding them in old chats, but the apps require an internet connection and are unavailable on Linux, the web and mobile devices. Anthropic says the feature is unavailable to HIPAA-ready organizations and hybrid deployments; Enterprise administrators must enable it.",
