      "title": "King tides collapse Pacifica pier as California coast floods",
      "content_html": "King tides and powerful surf tore part of the Pacifica Municipal Pier into the ocean on Wednesday, Nov. 25, as floodwaters reached beachfront homes in the Northern California city. The 1,140-foot pier had been closed during the summer after officials found cracks in its structure.\n\nFlooding also closed roads in Pacifica’s Sharp Park neighborhood, where some residents left with their pets; Marin County officials lifted an evacuation warning for Stinson Beach later Wednesday but urged people to stay away from the shore. The National Weather Service warned that waves could reach 20 to 30 feet and issued coastal flood alerts, with one Bay Area warning extended through 4 p.m. Thursday.",
